</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A3.3 </span>Reducing inference time with KV Cache</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During the iterative denoising process, the latents of memory and history frames are passed with a constant noise level <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since it does not change during this process, we compute the cache of key-value vectors of memory and history latents at the first denoising step.
In Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A3.2 Quantitative Results ‣ Appendix A3 Additional World Model Evaluation Results ‣ WEAVER, Better, Faster, Longer: An Effective World Model for Robotic Manipulation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we report that KV Cache can reduce inference time by up to 30%.</p>
</div>
